<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19241" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">galla</span></b> , ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Oak-apple</i>, <i>gall-nut</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 6,
				9, § 26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">24, 4, 5, § 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 9, 13,
				7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 3, §
				225</span></i>.—<i>Plur.</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 6, 7,
			2</span></i>. —In a pun with Galla, <i>a female
				Gaul;</i> v. 1. Galli, I.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A harsh</i>, <i>inferior kind of
			wine</i>, Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 445, 18</span></i>;
			cf. Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 96</span></i> Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
